From d125300aea501d52cc94690bacd87d9ab342311c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:00:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] macOS-like slider, joined keys, keys without a box, render
 timing

The slider now looks like the macOS one: a capsule (SliderWidth, default
720 px) that ends where the button that opened it starts, with a low and a
high icon (SliderIconLow / SliderIconHigh of that button) around an 8 px
track, filled in SliderFillColor up to a white key-high knob, and a round
light-grey close button in the button's place; the rest of the bar goes
dark, and a touch outside the capsule closes it. While the knob moves only
the capsule is sent to the panel.

Joined = true draws a button as one capsule with the one before it:
JoinedSpacing apart, the gap in SeparatorColor, only the outer corners
round (the collapsed Control Strip). Background = false leaves out the box
and draws only the icon.

TINY_DFR_RENDER_BENCH=<n> with TINY_DFR_RENDER_PNG times n frames of full
rows, a pressed key and the slider (drawing and the copy to a frame buffer,
not the USB transfer).

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
